== 4. Does the paired interval exclude the bulk effect? ======== 
  CRITERION (fixed before the numbers): 
    EXCLUDED   = bulk point estimate outside the Visium interval AND 
                 the two intervals do not overlap 
    CONSISTENT = the intervals overlap; the Visium data are 
                 underpowered to adjudicate, and that is the claim 
 
  RASSF9  --  Visium paired interval 0.56x to 2.40x 
    GSE112509  bulk 0.45x [0.31, 0.65] -> point inside Visium CI: FALSE | intervals overlap: TRUE  | CONSISTENT 
    GSE98394   bulk 0.45x [0.33, 0.61] -> point inside Visium CI: FALSE | intervals overlap: TRUE  | CONSISTENT 
 
  RASSF10  --  Visium paired interval 0.46x to 2.14x 
    GSE112509  bulk 0.44x [0.28, 0.68] -> point inside Visium CI: FALSE | intervals overlap: TRUE  | CONSISTENT 
 
  WHAT EACH VERDICT LICENSES: 
    EXCLUDED   -> the paired within-lesion design rules out a 
                  melanocyte-intrinsic effect of the size the bulk 
                  cohort reported. The bulk difference must come 
                  substantially from something other than the 
                  melanocytes, which is the composition explanation. 
    CONSISTENT -> the paired design cannot distinguish the two 
                  explanations. Report the interval and say so. 
                  Do NOT report it as evidence of no effect. 
 
  GSE112509 CARRIES THE MOST WEIGHT: both its arms are laser- 
  microdissected, so it is the bulk cohort least exposed to the 
  composition confound and the closest analogue to the Visium 
  design. Its verdicts: 
    RASSF9: CONSISTENT 
    RASSF10: CONSISTENT 

